From 43960c1f5fc549b1da607b2384f8390e4cdb1be4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pliskin Industrie <pliskin-industrie@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:32:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] power: supply: sm5714-fg: fix units and report capacity

The driver masked the SRAM values to 11 bits and interpreted them as
8.8 fixed point, so voltage_now reported ~0.5 V and current_now was in
mA without sign. Use the scaling of the vendor driver instead:

  VBAT     2700 mV +/- raw * 10 / 109 mV (sign/magnitude)
  OCV      raw / 2048 V
  CURRENT  raw / 2044 A, sign/magnitude, x2.5 in high range
  TEMP     raw * 10 * 2989 >> 19 (0.1 degC)

Report values in uV/uA as required by the power_supply ABI (current
positive while charging), serialise the SRAM address/data access, and
add voltage_avg/ocv, current_avg, charge_full(_design), charge_now,
energy_* and design voltages from the monitored-battery node (falling
back to 7040 mAh).

Scaling taken from the Samsung SM7125 vendor kernel
(drivers/battery/fuelgauge/sm5714_fuelgauge.c, GPL-2.0).

Signed-off-by: Pliskin Industrie <pliskin-industrie@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 52d9995d6c65d63ce90f4b70c5a4453fd8ab03b0)
